 "intro": "By the river Lycus in Lesser Armenia, 66 BC. You are Gnaeus Pompeius Magnus, given supreme command against Mithridates, who is retreating through the mountains.",
 "debrief": "In Plutarch’s and Cassius Dio’s accounts, Pompey got ahead of Mithridates and seized the heights above his route, then attacked his camp at night. The moon was low behind the Romans, throwing their shadows far ahead, so that the Pontic soldiers misjudged the distance and threw their javelins at shadows. The Pontic army was destroyed in the valley. Mithridates escaped with a few companions, including Hypsicratea, and Tigranes refused to shelter him. Pompey founded Nicopolis, ‘City of Victory’, nearby. The other choices are what-ifs.",
